NAME
       ballerina-clean - Remove the artifacts created during the build

SYNOPSIS
       bal clean [OPTIONS]


DESCRIPTION
       Remove the 'target' directory created during the build. This will delete
       all files and directories in the target directory.

       The default target directory that will be cleaned is the
       '<project-root>/target'. You may also provide a custom target to be cleaned.

       Additionally, the caches of the dependencies of the current package or
       workspace can also be cleaned.

       Compiled dependencies are cached in the user home and shared by all
       projects. Use '--prune-dependency-cache' to remove the ones that no build
       used for a number of days.


OPTIONS
       --target-dir <path>
           Target directory path.

       --dependency-cache
           Clean the caches of the dependencies of the current package
           or workspace. Packages in the local repository are kept, and only
           their compiled caches are removed. After republishing a version to
           the local repository, run this in each project that uses it.

       --prune-dependency-cache
           Remove the compiled dependencies that no build used for a number
           of days, from the caches of all projects. This does not clean the
           current package or workspace.

       --unused-days <days>
           Number of days without use after which '--prune-dependency-cache'
           removes a compiled dependency. The default is 30. '0' removes all
           compiled dependencies.

EXAMPLES
       Clean the default target directory of the current package or workspace.
           $ bal clean

       Clean the provided target directory.
           $ bal clean --target-dir <target-directory-path>

       Clean the caches of the dependencies of the current package or workspace,
       e.g. after republishing a version to the local repository.
           $ bal clean --dependency-cache

       Remove the compiled dependencies that no build used for 30 days.
           $ bal clean --prune-dependency-cache

       Remove the compiled dependencies that no build used for 7 days.
           $ bal clean --prune-dependency-cache --unused-days 7
